Build and load @ff-labs/fff-bun on FreeBSD.

fff-bun is the first thing opencode fails on under FreeBSD, before anything
else gets a chance to break:

  error: Cannot find module '@ff-labs/fff-bun'
      from packages/core/src/filesystem/fff.bun.ts

Two separate reasons, both fixed here:

  1. package.json's "os" list omits freebsd, so bun/npm skip installing the
     package entirely.
  2. getTriple() in src/platform.ts throws "Unsupported platform: freebsd"
     before any lookup happens. It is called from getNpmPackageName(), which
     findBinary() calls OUTSIDE its try/catch in the production path, so the
     throw escapes rather than degrading to "no prebuilt, use the dev build".

The native library itself needs no patch: `cargo build --release -p fff-c`
builds crates/fff-c (crate-type = cdylib) cleanly on FreeBSD as-is, producing
target/release/libfff_c.so. Only the JS-side platform plumbing was wrong.

The two triples added to TRIPLE_TO_NPM_PACKAGE point at @ff-labs/fff-bin-
freebsd-{x64,arm64}, which do not exist on npm. That is deliberate and
harmless: resolveFromNpmPackage() swallows the resolution failure and
findBinary() falls through to the locally built library. Publishing those
packages upstream would make the mapping real; until then it just keeps the
lookup from throwing.

Verified on the dev VM (185, FreeBSD 15.1-RC2, bun 1.4.0, rustc 1.96.1):
libfff_c.so loads through bun:ffi and FileFinder.create() + fileSearch()
return 100 real hits with git status and file metadata over a live tree.
aarch64 is listed but NOT built or tested here.

diff --git a/packages/fff-bun/package.json b/packages/fff-bun/package.json
index ec5ff07..4813048 100644
--- a/packages/fff-bun/package.json
+++ b/packages/fff-bun/package.json
@@ -33,7 +33,8 @@
     "darwin",
     "linux",
     "win32",
-    "android"
+    "android",
+    "freebsd"
   ],
   "cpu": [
     "x64",
diff --git a/packages/fff-bun/src/platform.ts b/packages/fff-bun/src/platform.ts
index 11070e2..130661d 100644
--- a/packages/fff-bun/src/platform.ts
+++ b/packages/fff-bun/src/platform.ts
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ export function getTriple(): string {
     osName = detectLinuxLibc();
   } else if (platform === "win32") {
     osName = "pc-windows-msvc";
+  } else if (platform === "freebsd") {
+    osName = "unknown-freebsd";
   } else {
     throw new Error(`Unsupported platform: ${platform}`);
   }
@@ -110,6 +112,8 @@ const TRIPLE_TO_NPM_PACKAGE: Record<string, string> = {
   "x86_64-pc-windows-msvc": "@ff-labs/fff-bin-win32-x64",
   "aarch64-pc-windows-msvc": "@ff-labs/fff-bin-win32-arm64",
   "aarch64-linux-android": "@ff-labs/fff-bin-android-arm64",
+  "x86_64-unknown-freebsd": "@ff-labs/fff-bin-freebsd-x64",
+  "aarch64-unknown-freebsd": "@ff-labs/fff-bin-freebsd-arm64",
 };
 
